{
    "UniqueID": "hw_spiritsickness",
    "//SpiritSickness": "Feature 28, spirit sickness (plan section 28, pack Prompt 39): the third Harsh Wilds AFFLICTION, on the fleas chassis (Documentation/Design/Harsh_Wilds_As_Built.md 7.1; Documentation/Research/HarshWilds/afflictions.md sections 1.7 and 4). One VISIBLE GameStat, cap 288, BaseRatePerTick 0, three statuses of 96 on vanilla sprites (Focus, MindState_Old, Headache_Old), alerts Low, Moderate and High. Its SOURCE is data-backed (afflictions.md section 4 test; wave0-spirits.md section 3, W0-19): a spirit that Harsh Wilds itself calls and angers. SelfTriggeredAction/Tgr_HW_SpiritSickness rolls, once a game day per spirit, while hw_event_lynx_spirit_angry, hw_event_goat_spirit_angry or hw_event_blood_spirit_angry is on the board (a CardType 3 card stays until its Continue is pressed), adding HW_SPIRIT_PER_ANGER = 96 (one band) when the roll picks Sick. Vanilla's Earth, Darkness and Fear spirits are NOT sources (their anger is already a curse or a mark) and no vanilla spirit is: whether a vanilla CT3 event card can gate an STA was not measured. CURE: the Cleansing Smudge (CardData/Item/hw_exorcism_smudge, the exorcism, a rite at a lit fire, -96, one stage); there is deliberately no time cure (a Repeat cooldown plays on the first tick the gate opens, which would wipe each sickness at once); Tgr_HW_SpiritSwitchOff clears the stat while the [Threats] SpiritSickness switch is off. Every write is a multiple of 96, so the stat lands only on 0, 96, 192 and 288, and every trigger on it starts at 1 ([clamp-own] in Development_Tools/Tests/HarshWilds-Afflictions.Tests.ps1). COST, statuses only, global modifiers clamped on read: vanilla Focus (4c5ed70723dc40e439720acab06e6af7, 0 to 96, base 48) VALUE -HW_SPIRIT_FOCUS_1..3 = -10, -20, -30; vanilla Stress RATE +0.25, +0.5, +0.75 a tick. A Focus value is used, not a rate, because Focus's own base rate is -2 and a negative rate could pin it at 0, where vanilla's lowest Focus status adds more Stress. Focus is watched by NO vanilla SelfTriggeredAction (export scan 2026-10-11), so no value lands on a trigger edge; vanilla's own Focus statuses (1 to 24 lowers Gratification and adds Stress +0.25) are the chain, counted by [clamp-rate] from Focus's base 48: stage 3 puts it at 18, so Stress net = base -0.25, own band -1.0, +0.75, +0.25 chain = -0.25, below 0, so spirit sickness alone never pins Stress at 240. Every number is a TUNABLE PLACEHOLDER, session-inferred and unmeasured against play.",
